  {
   "id": "Wdyp-RB3AwAJ",
   "from": "Yuchao Jiang",
   "author": "94ec915e8ce36448",
   "date": "2016-11-05T03:00:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: [canopy_phylogeny] Canopy.post error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi William,<div><br></div><div>The error that you saw was due to the fact that your MCMC has not converged yet. See the attached likelihood from 20 chains (4 were stuck in local mode). You need to let the chain run longer to get it converged. With the current thinning and binning that you have, the posterior tree space have way too many configurations (because the chain is still sampling and accepting jumps) and the NULL cutoff tree configuration frequency is 0.05. As a result, all of your posterior configurations have frequencies &lt; 0.05. A very quick fix to get a maximum-likelihood tree is to set post.config.cutoff = 0.01 but I would STRONGLY recommend that you sample longer.</div><div><br></div><div>I will update our website/package to give warnings/notes on this. Thanks for bringing this into our attention. Let me know if you have any questions.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Yuchao</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">--</font></div><font color=\"#000000\">Yuchao Jiang (<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@mail.med.upenn.edu</a>)</font><div><font color=\"#000000\">PhD student in Genomics and Computational Biology</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">University of Pennsylvania</font></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Nov 4, 2016 at 2:25 PM, Yuan, William <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">willia...@g.harvard.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div>Hi Yuchao, <br><br></div>I updated the package yesterday, so it should probably contain the updates you mentioned. Is there an older version that I should revert to and test? <br></div>I&#39;ve attached my .RData file, thank you so much for your help!<br><br></div>Best wishes,<br></div>William <br></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Nov 4, 2016 at 12:13 PM, Yuchao Jiang <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yj...@cornell.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi William,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your interest in Canopy! May I know when you updated your package from GitHub? I pushed some updates last week to fix bugs in Canopy.post -- the error might be due to this update. If you&#39;ve updated fairly recently, could you use save.image() to save your workspace? I can help you look into this.</div><div><br></div><div>Yuchao</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">--</font></div><font color=\"#000000\">Yuchao Jiang (<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@mail.med.upenn.edu</a>)</font><div><font color=\"#000000\">PhD student in Genomics and Computational Biology</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">University of Pennsylvania</font></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
